Package: burden
Title: Sample-Size-Adjusted Differential Expression Burden for Single-Cell Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ethan", "Fenton", email = "ethanfenton27@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates a sample-size-adjusted "burden" metric for
    differential expression (DE) results from single-cell data, addressing
    the fact that cell types with more cells tend to show more significant
    DE genes for reasons of statistical power alone. Works by downsampling
    cells per cell type, refitting DE at a range of cell counts, modeling
    the number of DEGs as a function of cell count (optionally with a
    spline/GAM term, with an automatic test for whether nonlinearity is
    needed), assessing concordance of downsampled DE calls against the
    full-data DE call, testing whether a pooled (across cell type) or
    cell-type-specific model is warranted, and predicting the expected DEG
    count at a common reference cell count. Also supports empirical
    FDR-calibrated per-sample-size significance thresholds as an
    alternative to a fixed alpha. DE backends are pluggable, with built-in
    wrappers for Wilcoxon rank-sum, edgeR, and DESeq2.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
